<h4 class="boldbyline">
Re: A Drunken Night In Iraq
</h4>

<p>
Contrast this story with Kruse's. This is why I love narrative. This one is not all that literary,  pretty much a just-the-facts account of a big story. It is the importance and the massive amount of reporting here that compel us to read on. With Kruse's story, the event he recounts could easily have been forgotten or ignored if not for a masterful performance by a great writer dealing with a much more subtle pile of information. <br />
<br />
Good work on both.
</p>
